-- title:
--   Unitary Conj Sum Eq One
-- statement:
--   **Unitary conjugation preserves a complete identity decomposition.** Let a finite family of operators `P b` sum to the identity, and let `U` be unitary. Conjugating every member by `U` preserves the sum:
--
--   $$
--   \sum_b P_b=I
--   \Longrightarrow
--   \sum_b U^{\dagger}P_bU=I.
--   $$
--
--   Together with preservation of projectivity, this identity shows that a unitary change of representation turns a projective measurement into another complete projective measurement.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.unitary_conj_sum_eq_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
